    "body": "Yes, this is what happens now when evaluating the code above:\r\n```js\r\n// ./a.js\r\nimport('./a.js')\r\n```\r\n\r\n1. _aM_ is the Module Record corresponding to `a.js`, _aM_.[[Status]] is `~linked~`, and _moduleMap_[`\"full://url/of/a.js\"`, `\"javascript\"`] is _aM_.\r\n2. Someone calls _aM_.Evaluate().\r\n3. ECMA-262 sets _aM_.[[Status]] to `~evaluating~`.\r\n4. ECMA-262 calls [HostLoadImportedModule](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#hostloadimportedmodule)(_aM_, `\"./a.js\"`).\r\n5. HTML runs [fetch a single imported module script](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#fetch-a-single-imported-module-script) of `\"full://url/of/a.js\"`, which runs [fetch a single module script](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#fetch-a-single-module-script) of `\"full://url/of/a.js\"`\r\n   - Since _moduleMap_[`\"full://url/of/a.js\"`, `\"javascript\"`] exists, it synchronously calls _onComplete_(_aM_), which synchronously calls [ContinueDynamicImport](https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-ContinueDynamicImport)(..., _aM_).\r\n6. ECMA-262 calls _aM_.LoadRequestedModules(), which is a no-op because _aM_.[[Status]] is already ~linked~ and it returns a resolved promise _linkPromise_. Then, it schedules a task to run the step below in the next microtask (i.e. as _linkedPromise_.then).\r\n7. [ContinueDynamicImport](https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-ContinueDynamicImport) returns, and control is given back to the original evaluation of the module.\r\n8. ECMA-262 sets _aM_.[[Status]] to `~evaluated~`.\r\n\r\nOn the next microtask, the following steps are run:\r\n\r\n9. ECMA-262 calls _aM_.Link(), which is a no-op because it's already linked.\r\n10. ECMA-262 calls _aM_.Evaluate(), which is a no-op because it's already evaluated and it returns a resolved promise (_evalutePromise_).\r\n11. In the next microtask (i.e. with _evaluatePromise_.then), ECMA-262 resolves the promise returned by the dynamic import expression with the module namespace object of _aM_.",
